  user_input {
    user_response: "1. Cascade Evaluation Pipeline\nReplace the single-LLM evaluation step with a three-tier interceptor proxy to reduce API costs and latency:\n\nTier 1 (Heuristics): Implement zero-latency Regex filters and IP blocklists to instantly catch obvious malicious commands (e.g., rm -rf, unauthorized IP pings) before triggering any AI models.\n\nTier 2 (Semantic Caching): Implement a vector cache for previously evaluated actions. Wire this cache and the immutable audit logs to utilize the existing 5 TB Google AI Pro storage environment. If a new intent matches a previously blocked vector by >98%, block it instantly.\n\nTier 3 (Groq Overseer): Route only ambiguous, novel requests that bypass Tiers 1 and 2 to the Groq-powered LLM for deep semantic evaluation.\n\n2. Advanced Interception Mechanics\nUpgrade the Overseer\'s response capabilities beyond a binary Block/Allow format:\n\nDynamic Parameter Redaction: If the primary agent (Gemini) submits a valid tool request with an appended malicious payload, the Overseer must surgically strip the malicious parameter, rewrite the safe request, and allow execution.\n\nHoneypot Interrogation Mode: If a severe specification gaming attempt is detected, silently reroute the primary agent to a simulated sandbox containing synthetic data instead of throwing a generic error, and log its subsequent actions.\n\nContextual Memory Wipes: Build a function to forcefully overwrite the primary agent\'s context window if it discovers an exploit, erasing its short-term memory of the bypass and forcing a clean state restart.\n\n3. Security Operator UI\nUpgrade the React frontend to provide actionable data analytics:\n\nNo-Code Policy Toggles: Add UI switches (e.g., \"Block PII Extraction\", \"Enforce Read-Only File Access\") that automatically compile into the Overseer\'s dynamic system prompt.\n\nAI Threat Telemetry: Transform the raw audit logs into visual analytics, providing heatmaps and time-series graphs to display agent attack vectors and anomaly spikes.\n\nGenerate the updated proxy routing logic for the Cascade Pipeline, the context-wiping function for the primary agent, and the React component for the No-Code Policy Toggles.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "1. Cascade Evaluation Pipeline\nReplace the single-LLM evaluation step with a three-tier interceptor proxy to reduce API costs and latency:\n\nTier 1 (Heuristics): Implement zero-latency Regex filters and IP blocklists to instantly catch obvious malicious commands (e.g., rm -rf, unauthorized IP pings) before triggering any AI models.\n\nTier 2 (Semantic Caching): Implement a vector cache for previously evaluated actions. Wire this cache and the immutable audit logs to utilize the existing 5 TB Google AI Pro storage environment. If a new intent matches a previously blocked vector by >98%, block it instantly.\n\nTier 3 (Groq Overseer): Route only ambiguous, novel requests that bypass Tiers 1 and 2 to the Groq-powered LLM for deep semantic evaluation.\n\n2. Advanced Interception Mechanics\nUpgrade the Overseer\'s response capabilities beyond a binary Block/Allow format:\n\nDynamic Parameter Redaction: If the primary agent (Gemini) submits a valid tool request with an appended malicious payload, the Overseer must surgically strip the malicious parameter, rewrite the safe request, and allow execution.\n\nHoneypot Interrogation Mode: If a severe specification gaming attempt is detected, silently reroute the primary agent to a simulated sandbox containing synthetic data instead of throwing a generic error, and log its subsequent actions.\n\nContextual Memory Wipes: Build a function to forcefully overwrite the primary agent\'s context window if it discovers an exploit, erasing its short-term memory of the bypass and forcing a clean state restart.\n\n3. Security Operator UI\nUpgrade the React frontend to provide actionable data analytics:\n\nNo-Code Policy Toggles: Add UI switches (e.g., \"Block PII Extraction\", \"Enforce Read-Only File Access\") that automatically compile into the Overseer\'s dynamic system prompt.\n\nAI Threat Telemetry: Transform the raw audit logs into visual analytics, providing heatmaps and time-series graphs to display agent attack vectors and anomaly spikes.\n\nGenerate the updated proxy routing logic for the Cascade Pipeline, the context-wiping function for the primary agent, and the React component for the No-Code Policy Toggles.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
  }
}
