  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting this user request for a \"cascade evaluation pipeline.\" My focus is on the proposed three-tier interceptor proxy and how it aims to optimize the evaluation process. The initial heuristics, like Regex filters and IP blocklists, are particularly interesting, especially their goal of instant detection of obvious malicious commands to minimize costs and reduce latency. My next step will be to model the implications of this approach.\n\n\n**Refining the Interception**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the interception mechanics. The dynamic parameter redaction is intriguing, presenting a nuanced alternative to simple blocking. Also, the honeypot interrogation mode offers a sophisticated approach to handling severe gaming attempts. I\'m exploring how these mechanisms can be seamlessly integrated to enhance security without hindering legitimate requests. I\'ll need to model the overhead of these advanced methods to determine their appropriate usage context.\n\n\n**Implementing Context Protection**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a new function. My current plan involves creating a function that will forcibly overwrite the primary agent\'s context window whenever an exploit is detected. This effectively erases its memory of the bypass and instigates a clean restart. I\'m also preparing the design for a React frontend, which will include no-code policy toggles and AI threat telemetry to provide actionable data analytics. I\'m moving toward generating the updated proxy routing logic.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
