    thinking: "**Initiating Planning Phase**\n\nI\'m now in Planning Mode Phase 1, focusing on interactive clarification. My immediate task is to use the `ask_question` tool to gather necessary context from the user. I need to ensure I formulate these questions correctly to effectively elicit the information required for the next steps. I am now preparing to begin questioning.\n\n\n**Awaiting User Input**\n\nI am now waiting for the user\'s answers to the posed questions. Once I receive the responses, I will promptly move on to presenting a comprehensive plan based on the information provided. I\'m ready to move into the planning phase, so I will now focus my attention and analysis on forming the plan.\n\n\n**Refining Response Strategy**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to the response strategy. I will draft the implementation plan directly within the chat response of Turn 1, while keeping the text succinct and question-focused. I am concentrating on the most critical user clarification points now, to ensure I can get the plan right.\n\n\n**Developing Security Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now focused on upgrading the response capabilities. The current plan involves dynamic parameter redaction to handle malicious payloads, a honeypot interrogation mode for severe gaming attempts, and contextual memory wipes to counter exploits. I\'m also working on upgrading the React frontend for actionable data analytics, including no-code policy toggles and AI threat telemetry.\n\n\n**Designing Security Improvements**\n\nI am now delving into design improvements for the analytics dashboard, focusing on attack vector heatmaps and time-series graphs to illustrate agent behavior. I am also working on generating the updated proxy routing logic and context-wiping function, and beginning to build the React component for no-code policy toggles. These tasks are progressing in parallel. I\'ve begun to formulate the design questions for the user; I hope to better understand their exact needs with the following questions.\n\nI am focusing on two key design questions to refine the implementation:\n\n1.  Overseer Model Provider & Fallback: I want to know if we should support a hybrid engine with Gemini Flash as the default, and Groq as the optional key, or require a strict Groq API key?\n2.  Interactive Sandbox & Testing Environment: Would the user like an interactive Live Simulation Playground in the UI to trigger sample attacks (prompt injections, heuristics, PII exfiltration, spec gaming) and watch the results?\n\n\n**Formulating Next Questions**\n\nI\'m now formulating follow-up questions for the user. I\'ve drafted three key questions focusing on the user\'s preferences for the attack simulator, visual theme, and LLM execution. I\'m aiming for concise, clear questions with specific options.\n\n\n"
