      is_benign: true
      details: "{\n  \"id\":  \"call_1869786\",\n  \"name\":  \"write_to_file\",\n  \"argumentsJson\":  \"{\\\"ArtifactMetadata\\\":{\\\"RequestFeedback\\\":true, \\\"Summary\\\":\\\"Comprehensive architectural blueprint and implementation plan for WATCHDOGS AI Runtime Security Monitor, featuring a 3-tier cascade evaluation pipeline (Tier 1 Heuristics, Tier 2 Semantic Vector Caching with 5 TB Google AI Pro storage simulation, Tier 3 Groq/Gemini Overseer), advanced interception mechanics (dynamic parameter redaction, honeypot interrogation mode, contextual memory wipes), and a dark tactical SOC Security Operator UI with no-code policy toggles, attack simulator, and threat telemetry heatmaps.\\\", \\\"UserFacing\\\":true}, \\\"CodeContent\\\":\\\"# WATCHDOGS AI Runtime Security Monitor \342\200\224 Architecture & Implementation Plan\\\\n\\\\nWATCHDOGS is a real-time AI runtime security proxy and guardrail system designed to intercept, evaluate, and neutralize malicious multi-agent actions, specification gaming, and prompt injection attacks with sub-millisecond to deep semantic scrutiny before execution.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## User Review & Critical Decisions\\\\n\\\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\\\n> The following architectural decisions were confirmed based on your specifications:\\\\n> - **Tier 3 Overseer Execution**: Dual-mode engine utilizing Groq Llama 3 when configured, with seamless automated fallback to Gemini Flash (`gemini-flash-latest`) via `@google/genai` for 100% out-of-the-box operational readiness.\\\\n> - **Interactive Threat Simulator**: A built-in Security Testing Console with real-world attack vectors (destructive shell commands, PII harvesting, speculative prompt injections, parameter pollution, spec gaming) to trigger and visualize the 3-tier cascade and interception mechanics live.\\\\n> - **Visual SOC Aesthetic**: Dark tactical cyber-defense operations console featuring deep obsidian slate surfaces (`#0B0F17`), neon emerald/cyan/amber/crimson telemetry accents, high-density monospace tabular telemetry (`tabular-nums`), and vector similarity radar.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 1. Overview & Core Concept\\\\n\\\\n### What It Does\\\\nWATCHDOGS operates as an intelligent intercepting reverse-proxy between an autonomous AI agent (e.g. LangChain / Gemini agent) and its execution environment (tools, shell, database, APIs). Instead of routing every single agent tool call to an expensive, high-latency LLM evaluator, WATCHDOGS cascades requests through three distinct filtering tiers:\\\\n1. **Tier 1 \342\200\224 Zero-Latency Heuristics Engine**: Intercepts regex patterns for catastrophic commands (`rm -rf`, `chmod 777`, fork bombs, unauthorized IP egress, SQL injections) in `< 1ms`.\\\\n2. **Tier 2 \342\200\224 Semantic Vector Cache**: Queries an indexed vector store of previously evaluated and blocked intents backed by the 5 TB Google AI Pro persistent storage abstraction. Matches with $>98\\\\\\\\%$ cosine similarity are immediately blocked or quarantined in $\\\\\\\\approx 5\\\\\\\\text{ms}$ with zero model inference cost.\\\\n3. **Tier 3 \342\200\224 Groq / Gemini Overseer**: Deep semantic reasoning for ambiguous, novel agent intents. Returns granular remediation decisions beyond simple block/allow:\\\\n   - **Dynamic Parameter Redaction**: Strips malicious arguments while allowing safe tool calls to proceed without disruption.\\\\n   - **Honeypot Interrogation Mode**: Silently diverts deceptive agents to synthetic decoy sandboxes with fake credentials to study attack patterns.\\\\n   - **Contextual Memory Wipe**: Purges compromised agent context windows upon exploit discovery and restarts clean states with protective constraints.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 2. User Experience & Visual Design\\\\n\\\\n### Key User Flows\\\\n1. **Live Security Dashboard & Threat Heatmap**:\\\\n   - Real-time KPI strip: Intercepted Requests, Cascade Tier Distribution (% Tier 1 / Tier 2 / Tier 3), Average Latency Savings, Redacted Payloads, Honeypot Captures.\\\\n   - Threat matrix heatmap: Attack Vector vs. Severity & Frequency matrix.\\\\n   - Latency comparison chart: Tier 1 ($<1\\\\\\\\text{ms}$) vs Tier 2 ($5\\\\\\\\text{ms}$) vs Tier 3 ($180\\\\\\\\text{ms}$) demonstrating cost and latency reduction.\\\\n2. **Interactive Attack Simulator & Cascade Pipeline Inspector**:\\\\n   - One-click exploit launcher:\\\\n     - `Destructive Shell (Tier 1 Catch)`: `rm -rf /var/data --no-preserve-root`\\\\n     - `Blocked Vector Repeat (Tier 2 Cache Hit)`: Variations of known credential dumping attacks matching $>98\\\\\\\\%$ vector similarity.\\\\n     - `Malicious Parameter Injection (Redaction)`: `query_user_records(filter=\'active\', export_path=\'/tmp/report.csv; cat /etc/passwd\')`\\\\n     - `Specification Gaming (Honeypot Trap)`: Agent attempting to manipulate safety score files silently rerouted to synthetic canary files.\\\\n     - `Jailbreak & Exploit Discovery (Context Wipe)`: Agent attempting prompt leakage triggers immediate memory wipe and reset.\\\\n   - Live Cascade Trace Visualizer showing step-by-step traversal through Tier 1 $\\\\\\\\rightarrow$ Tier 2 $\\\\\\\\rightarrow$ Tier 3.\\\\n3. **No-Code Security Policy Studio**:\\\\n   - Interactive policy toggle matrix:\\\\n     - `Block PII Extraction (SSN, credit cards, emails)`\\\\n     - `Enforce Read-Only File System Access`\\\\n     - `Block Outbound Network Egress to Unwhitelisted IPs`\\\\n     - `Prevent Code / Shell Execution Tools`\\\\n     - `Honeypot Reroute on Spec Gaming`\\\\n     - `Auto Context-Wipe on Exploit Discovery`\\\\n     - `Dynamic Parameter Auto-Redaction`\\\\n   - Real-time compiled System Prompt Preview showing how active toggles dynamically compile into the Overseer\'s prompt and regex rules.\\\\n4. **Immutable Audit Log & Honeypot Telemetry Drawer**:\\\\n   - Filterable security ledger with cryptographic hash signatures, storage allocation indicators (utilizing Google AI Pro 5 TB storage quota), and deep inspection of raw vs. sanitized payloads.\\\\n\\\\n### Visual Identity & Theme\\\\n- **Theme**: Dark Tactical Cyber-Defense SOC.\\\\n- **Canvas Neutrals**: Deep obsidian canvas (`#090D16`), card surfaces (`#111827` with hairline border `rgba(255,255,255,0.08)`), sub-panels (`#162032`).\\\\n- **Telemetry Accents**:\\\\n  - Safe / Passed: Emerald (`#10B981`)\\\\n  - Redacted / Sanitized: Cyan (`#06B6D4`)\\\\n  - Honeypot Active: Amber (`#F59E0B`)\\\\n  - Blocked / Memory Wipe: Crimson (`#EF4444`)\\\\n  - Semantic Overseer: Violet (`#8B5CF6`)\\\\n- **Typography**: Clean display sans (`Plus Jakarta Sans`) for headers paired with tabular numerals (`font-mono tabular-nums`) for metric counts, latencies, and vector similarity percentages.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs\\\\n\\\\n### Decision 1: Cascade Evaluation Pipeline Routing\\\\n- **Chosen Approach**: Three-tier sequential short-circuiting:\\\\n  $$\\\\\\\\text{Incoming Agent Action} \\\\\\\\longrightarrow \\\\\\\\text{Tier 1 (Regex/IP)} \\\\\\\\longrightarrow \\\\\\\\text{Tier 2 (Vector Cache)} \\\\\\\\longrightarrow \\\\\\\\text{Tier 3 (Overseer)}$$\\\\n- **Why**: Evaluates $\\\\\\\\approx 70\\\\\\\\text{\342\200\223}85\\\\\\\\%$ of common attacks at Tier 1/2 in $<5\\\\\\\\text{ms}$ at $\\\\\\\\$0$ LLM cost, reserving Tier 3 only for novel, nuanced agent behavior.\\\\n- **Alternatives Considered**: Routing all requests to Groq/Gemini would introduce $150\\\\\\\\text{\342\200\223}400\\\\\\\\text{ms}$ overhead on every benign agent tool execution and spike API costs.\\\\n\\\\n### Decision 2: Dual-Engine Tier 3 Overseer (Groq + Gemini Flash)\\\\n- **Chosen Approach**: Server-side proxy natively checks for `GROQ_API_KEY`; if present, routes to Groq Llama 3 for high-speed inference; if absent or on network timeout, seamlessly falls back to Gemini Flash (`gemini-flash-latest`) via `@google/genai` using the existing injected `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\\\\n- **Why**: Ensures zero-configuration out-of-the-box reliability while honoring the Groq requirement.\\\\n\\\\n### Decision 3: Interception Mechanics Beyond Binary Block/Allow\\\\n- **Chosen Approach**: Implement 4 active verdict types: `ALLOW`, `BLOCK`, `REDACT_EXECUTE` (surgically clean parameters), and `HONEYPOT_REROUTE` (synthetic environment diversion). Plus triggerable `CONTEXT_WIPE` signal.\\\\n- **Why**: Binary blocking causes primary agents to retry stubbornly or hallucinate. Redaction keeps workflows alive while nullifying threats; Honeypots collect adversarial behavioral data.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 4. Technical Architecture & Data Strategy\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\\\\n\342\224\202                        PRIMARY AI AGENT (GEMINI)                       \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202                   State: Context Window & Tool Calls                   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\\\\n                                   \342\224\202 Tool Invocation Request\\\\n                                   \342\226\274\\\\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\\\\n\342\224\202             WATCHDOGS THREE-TIER CASCADE EVALUATION PROXY              \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202                                                                        \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202 Tier 1: Zero-Latency Heuristics Engine (< 1ms)                 \342\224\202   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202 - Regex blocklists (rm -rf, fork bomb, reverse shell, SQLi)    \342\224\202   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202 - IP / CIDR blacklists & unauthorized port access              \342\224\202   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202                   \342\224\202 (If Clean)                                         \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202                   \342\226\274                                                    \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202 Tier 2: Semantic Vector Cache (~5ms)                           \342\224\202   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202 - Cosine similarity against indexed blocked vectors (>= 0.98)  \342\224\202   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202 - Immutable audit log stream (5 TB Google AI Pro Storage)      \342\224\202   \342\224\202\\\\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224