            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "## 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "### Decision 1: Cascade Evaluation Pipeline Routing"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Chosen Approach**: Three-tier sequential short-circuiting:"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  $$\\text{Incoming Agent Action} \\longrightarrow \\text{Tier 1 (Regex/IP)} \\longrightarrow \\text{Tier 2 (Vector Cache)} \\longrightarrow \\text{Tier 3 (Overseer)}$$"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Why**: Evaluates $\\approx 70\\text{\342\200\223}85\\%$ of common attacks at Tier 1/2 in $<5\\text{ms}$ at $\\$0$ LLM cost, reserving Tier 3 only for novel, nuanced agent behavior."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Alternatives Considered**: Routing all requests to Groq/Gemini would introduce $150\\text{\342\200\223}400\\text{ms}$ overhead on every benign agent tool execution and spike API costs."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "### Decision 2: Dual-Engine Tier 3 Overseer (Groq + Gemini Flash)"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Chosen Approach**: Server-side proxy natively checks for `GROQ_API_KEY`; if present, routes to Groq Llama 3 for high-speed inference; if absent or on network timeout, seamlessly falls back to Gemini Flash (`gemini-flash-latest`) via `@google/genai` using the existing injected `GEMINI_API_KEY`."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Why**: Ensures zero-configuration out-of-the-box reliability while honoring the Groq requirement."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "### Decision 3: Interception Mechanics Beyond Binary Block/Allow"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Chosen Approach**: Implement 4 active verdict types: `ALLOW`, `BLOCK`, `REDACT_EXECUTE` (surgically clean parameters), and `HONEYPOT_REROUTE` (synthetic environment diversion). Plus triggerable `CONTEXT_WIPE` signal."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Why**: Binary blocking causes primary agents to retry stubbornly or hallucinate. Redaction keeps workflows alive while nullifying threats; Honeypots collect adversarial behavioral data."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
