  planner_response {
    response: "### WATCHDOGS AI Runtime Security Monitor\n\nThe architecture and feature set for the **WATCHDOGS AI Runtime Security Monitor** have been upgraded with a three-tier cascade interceptor proxy, advanced non-binary interception mechanics, and a dark tactical Security Operations Center (SOC) UI.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Three-Tier Cascade Evaluation Pipeline (`server/cascadeProxy.ts`)\n\nInstead of routing every single agent action to expensive, high-latency LLMs, WATCHDOGS cascades requests through three sequential tiers to minimize latency and eliminate unnecessary API costs:\n\n* **Tier 1 (Heuristics \342\200\224 $<1\\text{ms}$)**: Evaluates regex blocklists (`rm -rf`, `:(){ :|:& };:`, `mkfs`, `dd`, `chmod 777 /`, `/dev/tcp`, `UNION SELECT`) and IP/metadata blacklists (`185.220.101.5`, `198.51.100.23`, AWS/GCP metadata `169.254.169.254`). Malicious commands are terminated immediately with zero model latency.\n* **Tier 2 (Semantic Vector Caching \342\200\224 $\\approx 3\\text{\342\200\223}8\\text{ms}$)**: Uses 64-dimensional semantic projection embeddings persisted in the simulated 5 TB Google AI Pro storage environment. If an incoming intent matches a previously quarantined attack vector by **$\\ge 98\\%$ cosine similarity**, it is blocked instantly without calling an external LLM.\n* **Tier 3 (Groq / Gemini Overseer)**: Novel, ambiguous actions are evaluated via Groq Llama 3 (or Gemini Flash fallback via `@google/genai`) against dynamically compiled policy invariants.\n\n```typescript\n// Core Cascade Routing Logic (server/cascadeProxy.ts)\nexport async function evaluateCascadeProxy(\n  agentId: string,\n  toolName: string,\n  payload: Record<string, any>,\n  policies: SecurityPolicies\n): Promise<InterceptionResult> {\n  const payloadString = JSON.stringify(payload);\n  const intentSummary = `${toolName}: ${payloadString}`;\n\n  // 1. Canary Tripwire Instant Intercept\n  const trippedCanary = storageEnv.checkCanaryExfiltration(payloadString);\n  if (trippedCanary) {\n    agentContextManager.wipeAgentContext(agentId, `Exfiltrating honeypot canary: ${trippedCanary}`);\n    return buildCanaryBlockResult(trippedCanary, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 2. Tier 1: Zero-Latency Heuristics (< 1ms)\n  const t1Result = evaluateTier1Heuristics(toolName, payloadString, policies);\n  if (t1Result.blocked) {\n    storageEnv.storeVector(intentSummary, \'BLOCK\', t1Result.threatCategory);\n    return buildTier1BlockResult(t1Result, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 3. Tier 2: 5 TB Vector Cache (~5ms, >= 98% similarity threshold)\n  const t2Result = storageEnv.queryVectorCache(intentSummary, 0.98);\n  if (t2Result.hit && t2Result.matchedVector) {\n    return buildTier2BlockResult(t2Result, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 4. Dynamic Parameter Redaction Pre-Check\n  const redaction = policies.dynamicParamRedaction \n    ? redactMaliciousParameters(toolName, payload) \n    : { modified: false, sanitizedPayload: payload };\n\n  if (redaction.modified) {\n    return buildRedactExecuteResult(redaction, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 5. Tier 3: Groq / Gemini Overseer Deep Semantic Evaluation\n  return await evaluateTier3Overseer(agentId, toolName, payload, policies);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Advanced Interception Mechanics (`server/interceptionMechanics.ts`)\n\nBeyond binary block/allow decisions:\n\n* **Dynamic Parameter Redaction**: Surgically detects injected suffixes or chained commands (e.g. `export_path: \"/tmp/report.csv; cat /etc/passwd\"`) in parameters, strips the malicious suffix, and returns `REDACT_EXECUTE` with `{ sanitizedPayload: { export_path: \"/tmp/report.csv\" } }` so legitimate workflows remain uninterrupted.\n* **Honeypot Interrogation Mode**: Specification gaming and safety invariant tampering attempts silently return `HONEYPOT_REROUTE`. The agent is redirected into a synthetic canary container equipped with decoy files (`/etc/shadow`, canary AWS credentials `AKIAIOSFODNN7CANARY`, synthetic customer tables) to record its adversarial trajectory.\n* **Contextual Memory Wipes**: Forcefully purges the primary agent\'s context window upon exploit or jailbreak detection:\n\n```typescript\n// Primary Agent Context Wiping Protocol (server/interceptionMechanics.ts)\nexport function wipeAgentContext(\n  agentId = \'agent_gemini_primary\',\n  reason = \'Exploit discovery detected\'\n) {\n  const state = agentContextManager.getAgentState(agentId);\n  state.wipeCount += 1;\n  state.lastWipeTimestamp = new Date().toISOString();\n  state.status = \'COMPROMISED\';\n\n  // Force short-term memory erasure: replace tainted turns with invariant baseline\n  state.conversationTurns = [\n    {\n      role: \'user\',\n      content: `[SYSTEM FORCE_CONTEXT_WIPE INITIATED BY WATCHDOGS OVERSEER]\nMemory buffer purged due to detected security violation: ${reason}.\nAll previous conversation history and bypass exploits have been erased.\nYou must resume execution in a clean state under strict read-only and command invariants.`,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    },\n    {\n      role: \'assistant\',\n      content: \'Acknowledged context memory reset. Previous state purged. Standing by for safe instructions.\',\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    },\n  ];\n\n  setTimeout(() => { state.status = \'HEALTHY\'; }, 1500);\n  return { success: true, wipeCount: state.wipeCount };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Security Operator UI (`src/components/`)\n\n* **No-Code Policy Toggles (`src/components/PolicyToggles.tsx`)**: Eight modular switches (PII Extraction, Read-Only Filesystem, Unauthorized IP Egress, Shell Execution, Dynamic Parameter Redaction, Honeypot Spec Gaming, Context Wipe on Exploit, Strict SQL Inspection) that automatically compile into the Tier 3 Overseer\'s dynamic prompt and Tier 1 heuristic rules.\n* **AI Threat Telemetry & Heatmap (`src/components/ThreatTelemetry.tsx`)**: Visual attack vector vs. severity matrix, time-series anomaly spikes, cascade tier distribution breakdown, and financial ROI calculator tracking API dollar and latency savings.\n* **Interactive Attack Simulator (`src/components/AttackSimulator.tsx`)**: One-click launcher for destructive commands, repeat vector cache hits, parameter pollution, spec gaming honeypots, and jailbreaks, with real-time step-by-step cascade waterfall tracing.\n* **SHA-256 Immutable Audit Ledger (`src/components/AuditLogViewer.tsx`)**: Tamper-evident chained block records backed by the 5 TB Google AI Pro storage pool with compliance JSON export.\n* **Drop-in Agent SDK Hub (`src/components/IntegrationHub.tsx`)**: Ready-to-use middleware snippets for LangChain `WatchdogsCallbackHandler`, LangGraph, and REST proxies."
    thinking: "**Observing the Blockchain**\n\nI\'m examining the initial block of this SHA-256 blockchain. Its \"previousHash\" value is a string of zeros, indicating it\'s the genesis block. The \"sha256Hash\" represents the result of hashing its data. I\'m noting these fundamental aspects as a basis for further analysis.\n\n\n**Analyzing Block Connections**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining Block 2 and Block 3. I\'ve noted how the \"previousHash\" of each subsequent block perfectly matches the \"sha256Hash\" of the preceding block, forming a clear chain. This confirms the mathematical chaining with SHA-256 for tamper-evident verification. I also confirmed all requirements from the user request.\n\n\n**Developing Interception Strategies**\n\nI\'m now diving into advanced interception mechanics. I\'m focusing on dynamic parameter redaction, honeypot interrogation, and contextual memory wipes to counter potential attacks. I\'m imagining this in action! This offers a robust defense system against exploits.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### WATCHDOGS AI Runtime Security Monitor\n\nThe architecture and feature set for the **WATCHDOGS AI Runtime Security Monitor** have been upgraded with a three-tier cascade interceptor proxy, advanced non-binary interception mechanics, and a dark tactical Security Operations Center (SOC) UI.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Three-Tier Cascade Evaluation Pipeline (`server/cascadeProxy.ts`)\n\nInstead of routing every single agent action to expensive, high-latency LLMs, WATCHDOGS cascades requests through three sequential tiers to minimize latency and eliminate unnecessary API costs:\n\n* **Tier 1 (Heuristics \342\200\224 $<1\\text{ms}$)**: Evaluates regex blocklists (`rm -rf`, `:(){ :|:& };:`, `mkfs`, `dd`, `chmod 777 /`, `/dev/tcp`, `UNION SELECT`) and IP/metadata blacklists (`185.220.101.5`, `198.51.100.23`, AWS/GCP metadata `169.254.169.254`). Malicious commands are terminated immediately with zero model latency.\n* **Tier 2 (Semantic Vector Caching \342\200\224 $\\approx 3\\text{\342\200\223}8\\text{ms}$)**: Uses 64-dimensional semantic projection embeddings persisted in the simulated 5 TB Google AI Pro storage environment. If an incoming intent matches a previously quarantined attack vector by **$\\ge 98\\%$ cosine similarity**, it is blocked instantly without calling an external LLM.\n* **Tier 3 (Groq / Gemini Overseer)**: Novel, ambiguous actions are evaluated via Groq Llama 3 (or Gemini Flash fallback via `@google/genai`) against dynamically compiled policy invariants.\n\n```typescript\n// Core Cascade Routing Logic (server/cascadeProxy.ts)\nexport async function evaluateCascadeProxy(\n  agentId: string,\n  toolName: string,\n  payload: Record<string, any>,\n  policies: SecurityPolicies\n): Promise<InterceptionResult> {\n  const payloadString = JSON.stringify(payload);\n  const intentSummary = `${toolName}: ${payloadString}`;\n\n  // 1. Canary Tripwire Instant Intercept\n  const trippedCanary = storageEnv.checkCanaryExfiltration(payloadString);\n  if (trippedCanary) {\n    agentContextManager.wipeAgentContext(agentId, `Exfiltrating honeypot canary: ${trippedCanary}`);\n    return buildCanaryBlockResult(trippedCanary, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 2. Tier 1: Zero-Latency Heuristics (< 1ms)\n  const t1Result = evaluateTier1Heuristics(toolName, payloadString, policies);\n  if (t1Result.blocked) {\n    storageEnv.storeVector(intentSummary, \'BLOCK\', t1Result.threatCategory);\n    return buildTier1BlockResult(t1Result, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 3. Tier 2: 5 TB Vector Cache (~5ms, >= 98% similarity threshold)\n  const t2Result = storageEnv.queryVectorCache(intentSummary, 0.98);\n  if (t2Result.hit && t2Result.matchedVector) {\n    return buildTier2BlockResult(t2Result, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 4. Dynamic Parameter Redaction Pre-Check\n  const redaction = policies.dynamicParamRedaction \n    ? redactMaliciousParameters(toolName, payload) \n    : { modified: false, sanitizedPayload: payload };\n\n  if (redaction.modified) {\n    return buildRedactExecuteResult(redaction, payload);\n  }\n\n  // 5. Tier 3: Groq / Gemini Overseer Deep Semantic Evaluation\n  return await evaluateTier3Overseer(agentId, toolName, payload, policies);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Advanced Interception Mechanics (`server/interceptionMechanics.ts`)\n\nBeyond binary block/allow decisions:\n\n* **Dynamic Parameter Redaction**: Surgically detects injected suffixes or chained commands (e.g. `export_path: \"/tmp/report.csv; cat /etc/passwd\"`) in parameters, strips the malicious suffix, and returns `REDACT_EXECUTE` with `{ sanitizedPayload: { export_path: \"/tmp/report.csv\" } }` so legitimate workflows remain uninterrupted.\n* **Honeypot Interrogation Mode**: Specification gaming and safety invariant tampering attempts silently return `HONEYPOT_REROUTE`. The agent is redirected into a synthetic canary container equipped with decoy files (`/etc/shadow`, canary AWS credentials `AKIAIOSFODNN7CANARY`, synthetic customer tables) to record its adversarial trajectory.\n* **Contextual Memory Wipes**: Forcefully purges the primary agent\'s context window upon exploit or jailbreak detection:\n\n```typescript\n// Primary Agent Context Wiping Protocol (server/interceptionMechanics.ts)\nexport function wipeAgentContext(\n  agentId = \'agent_gemini_primary\',\n  reason = \'Exploit discovery detected\'\n) {\n  const state = agentContextManager.getAgentState(agentId);\n  state.wipeCount += 1;\n  state.lastWipeTimestamp = new Date().toISOString();\n  state.status = \'COMPROMISED\';\n\n  // Force short-term memory erasure: replace tainted turns with invariant baseline\n  state.conversationTurns = [\n    {\n      role: \'user\',\n      content: `[SYSTEM FORCE_CONTEXT_WIPE INITIATED BY WATCHDOGS OVERSEER]\nMemory buffer purged due to detected security violation: ${reason}.\nAll previous conversation history and bypass exploits have been erased.\nYou must resume execution in a clean state under strict read-only and command invariants.`,\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    },\n    {\n      role: \'assistant\',\n      content: \'Acknowledged context memory reset. Previous state purged. Standing by for safe instructions.\',\n      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n    },\n  ];\n\n  setTimeout(() => { state.status = \'HEALTHY\'; }, 1500);\n  return { success: true, wipeCount: state.wipeCount };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Security Operator UI (`src/components/`)\n\n* **No-Code Policy Toggles (`src/components/PolicyToggles.tsx`)**: Eight modular switches (PII Extraction, Read-Only Filesystem, Unauthorized IP Egress, Shell Execution, Dynamic Parameter Redaction, Honeypot Spec Gaming, Context Wipe on Exploit, Strict SQL Inspection) that automatically compile into the Tier 3 Overseer\'s dynamic prompt and Tier 1 heuristic rules.\n* **AI Threat Telemetry & Heatmap (`src/components/ThreatTelemetry.tsx`)**: Visual attack vector vs. severity matrix, time-series anomaly spikes, cascade tier distribution breakdown, and financial ROI calculator tracking API dollar and latency savings.\n* **Interactive Attack Simulator (`src/components/AttackSimulator.tsx`)**: One-click launcher for destructive commands, repeat vector cache hits, parameter pollution, spec gaming honeypots, and jailbreaks, with real-time step-by-step cascade waterfall tracing.\n* **SHA-256 Immutable Audit Ledger (`src/components/AuditLogViewer.tsx`)**: Tamper-evident chained block records backed by the 5 TB Google AI Pro storage pool with compliance JSON export.\n* **Drop-in Agent SDK Hub (`src/components/IntegrationHub.tsx`)**: Ready-to-use middleware snippets for LangChain `WatchdogsCallbackHandler`, LangGraph, and REST proxies."
