  planner_response {
    response: "The UI/UX has been refined and a dedicated **Operational Guide & Defense Playbook** tab has been added to help operators, judges, and developers understand, demonstrate, and deploy WATCHDOGS.\n\n---\n\n### What\'s New & Refined\n\n#### 1. New Operational Guide Tab (`src/components/GuideTab.tsx`)\nA dedicated learning hub accessible directly from the top navigation and ribbon banner (`How It Works (Guide)`):\n* **1. Quick-Start (3 Steps)**: Visual explainer showing how WATCHDOGS drops in between agents and tools.\n* **2. The 3-Tier Cascade**: Interactive breakdown comparing Tier 1 Heuristics ($<1\\text{ms}$), Tier 2 Vector Caching ($3\\text{\342\200\223}8\\text{ms}$ on 5 TB Google AI Pro storage), and Tier 3 Overseer, complete with a latency and cost comparison matrix against traditional single-LLM guardrails.\n* **3. Interception Mechanics**: Deep dive into **Dynamic Parameter Redaction**, **Honeypot Interrogation Mode & Canary Tripwires**, and **Contextual Memory Wiping**.\n* **4. Live Demo Checklist**: Step-by-step checklist tailored for live presentations with direct **\"Test\"** links that jump straight to the Attack Simulator.\n* **5. Security FAQs**: Explaining vector similarity thresholds ($\\ge 98\\%$), LLM timeout resilience, and SOC 2 / EU AI Act cryptographic verification.\n\n#### 2. UI/UX Refinements Across the Platform\n* **Top Navigation Bar (`TopBar.tsx`)**: Unified single-row navigation with clear active state indicators and instant access to the emergency context wipe action.\n* **Ribbon Status Banner**: Added a **\"How It Works (Guide)\"** quick-launch button alongside live average latency and quick telemetry sync.\n* **Visual Hierarchy & Contrast**: Enforced 60-30-10 dark obsidian palette (`#070a11` / `#0b0f19`) with neon telemetry accents (cyan for heuristics/redaction, emerald for passes/vector cache, amber for honeypots, and crimson for blocks/memory wipes).\n* **Compliance Export Bar (`AuditLogViewer.tsx`)**: Direct buttons for **Export SOC 2 JSON** (with Merkle aggregate root signature) and **Export CSV** (with RFC 4180 SHA-256 header manifest)."
    modified_response: "The UI/UX has been refined and a dedicated **Operational Guide & Defense Playbook** tab has been added to help operators, judges, and developers understand, demonstrate, and deploy WATCHDOGS.\n\n---\n\n### What\'s New & Refined\n\n#### 1. New Operational Guide Tab (`src/components/GuideTab.tsx`)\nA dedicated learning hub accessible directly from the top navigation and ribbon banner (`How It Works (Guide)`):\n* **1. Quick-Start (3 Steps)**: Visual explainer showing how WATCHDOGS drops in between agents and tools.\n* **2. The 3-Tier Cascade**: Interactive breakdown comparing Tier 1 Heuristics ($<1\\text{ms}$), Tier 2 Vector Caching ($3\\text{\342\200\223}8\\text{ms}$ on 5 TB Google AI Pro storage), and Tier 3 Overseer, complete with a latency and cost comparison matrix against traditional single-LLM guardrails.\n* **3. Interception Mechanics**: Deep dive into **Dynamic Parameter Redaction**, **Honeypot Interrogation Mode & Canary Tripwires**, and **Contextual Memory Wiping**.\n* **4. Live Demo Checklist**: Step-by-step checklist tailored for live presentations with direct **\"Test\"** links that jump straight to the Attack Simulator.\n* **5. Security FAQs**: Explaining vector similarity thresholds ($\\ge 98\\%$), LLM timeout resilience, and SOC 2 / EU AI Act cryptographic verification.\n\n#### 2. UI/UX Refinements Across the Platform\n* **Top Navigation Bar (`TopBar.tsx`)**: Unified single-row navigation with clear active state indicators and instant access to the emergency context wipe action.\n* **Ribbon Status Banner**: Added a **\"How It Works (Guide)\"** quick-launch button alongside live average latency and quick telemetry sync.\n* **Visual Hierarchy & Contrast**: Enforced 60-30-10 dark obsidian palette (`#070a11` / `#0b0f19`) with neon telemetry accents (cyan for heuristics/redaction, emerald for passes/vector cache, amber for honeypots, and crimson for blocks/memory wipes).\n* **Compliance Export Bar (`AuditLogViewer.tsx`)**: Direct buttons for **Export SOC 2 JSON** (with Merkle aggregate root signature) and **Export CSV** (with RFC 4180 SHA-256 header manifest)."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
