  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Port Conflicts**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The error log is screaming about `EADDRINUSE` on port 8080. My immediate thought was, \"Why 8080?\" I\'m now digging into `server.ts` to trace where that port assignment originates. I\'m focusing on the `PORT` variable declaration, to understand how it\'s being set.\n\n\n**Clarifying Port Assignment**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough. I discovered Google Cloud Run sets `process.env.PORT` to 8080. However, the AI Studio dev server mandates port 3000 for the applet. The problem? My `server.ts` was naively using `process.env.PORT`, leading to a conflict with the internal supervisor. Now, I\'m updating `server.ts` to always listen on port 3000 during development to fix this. I am also planning on adding a production config.\n\n\n"
