  planner_response {
    response: "The dev server has been resolved and is now running on port 3000.\n\n### Cause of the Issue\n1. **Missing Module Dependencies**: `node_modules` needed a clean installation across all project packages (`express`, `tsx`, `@google/genai`, etc.).\n2. **Port Conflict (`EADDRINUSE`)**: In the AI Studio container environment, `process.env.PORT` was set to `8080` (used internally by the environment supervisor), causing `server.ts` to attempt binding to `0.0.0.0:8080` instead of port `3000`.\n\n### Fix Applied\n1. Installed all dependencies via `install_applet_dependencies`.\n2. Hardcoded the server listener in `server.ts` to explicitly bind to **port 3000** (`0.0.0.0:3000`) and disabled Vite HMR in `createViteServer` to avoid port collisions with the environment proxy.\n3. Verified compilation (`compile_applet`), TypeScript checks (`lint_applet`), and verified `HTTP 200 OK` responses from both `/api/health` and the frontend entry point."
    modified_response: "The dev server has been resolved and is now running on port 3000.\n\n### Cause of the Issue\n1. **Missing Module Dependencies**: `node_modules` needed a clean installation across all project packages (`express`, `tsx`, `@google/genai`, etc.).\n2. **Port Conflict (`EADDRINUSE`)**: In the AI Studio container environment, `process.env.PORT` was set to `8080` (used internally by the environment supervisor), causing `server.ts` to attempt binding to `0.0.0.0:8080` instead of port `3000`.\n\n### Fix Applied\n1. Installed all dependencies via `install_applet_dependencies`.\n2. Hardcoded the server listener in `server.ts` to explicitly bind to **port 3000** (`0.0.0.0:3000`) and disabled Vite HMR in `createViteServer` to avoid port collisions with the environment proxy.\n3. Verified compilation (`compile_applet`), TypeScript checks (`lint_applet`), and verified `HTTP 200 OK` responses from both `/api/health` and the frontend entry point."
